  "description": "The scene depicts a human skeleton as a visual metaphor for dehumanization, used to imply that Black people are inherently primitive or animal-like. The skeleton is positioned upright in dirt, and overlaid text reinforces the harmful stereotype that 'not all black people are criminals'. The visual and textual elements are directly related to create a racially charged message.",
